
A `var` declared in a component body is the component's state, and a `var`
declared in a window body has to compile to the same shape -- which is what
window_state_win.txtar asserts. This archive is the reference it is held
against: the same program written as a component, where the shape was never
in doubt.

html emits the same script for both, differing only in the generated-from
header and the title the window declares. That is the whole claim, so this
archive builds html alone.
-- comp.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

component main node {
    var n = 0
    vbox {
        text(value="{n}")
        button #inc(text="+", @click { n = n + 1 })
    }
}

window {
    main
}
